  "spec": "specs.md §7, §21.2",
  "description": "What a path of Atoll's own view presents, from the catalog's rows for it: the file and its copies, the entries of each disk, and the disks' positions and states. The disks that present are online, standby, readonly or draining, by position, then failed. The first disk that holds a copy ok or surplus that is at the path, its clock not running and its file's rename followed, or an entry, says what the path is. A cache disk presents nothing until phase 2b. A file presents its original, or the first copy on a failed disk; an entry presents the first disk's row. A folder's mode is then narrowed by every other folder at the path on a disk that presents, each as it would present alone: no caller is given, by its permission bits, what a disk's folder may refuse it there. A caller of the first's owner is, on that disk, of its owner when it is the same account, and otherwise of its group or of its others, as nothing says which groups an account is in; a caller of the first's group or of its others may be that disk's owner when it is another account, and is of that disk's group, or of its others, when the two folders have one group, or may be of either otherwise. Each class keeps the bits that every class it may be there gives. The sticky bit of any of them is presented; setuid and setgid are the first's, and so are the owner, the group, the size and the time. The view's own owner is 4242:4343. node is null when the path is absent.",
